ok - a delivered task leaves underway and the gates for one delivered row
ok - an armed merge watch does not retire a worker that is still working
ok - an underway row names its home and carries the request already recorded for it
ok - the delivered exit rule fires at its named threshold and is one-way
ok - the exit rule reads one named threshold, and the output states which
ok - an underway row from a second mate is distinguishable from main work in the same repo
ok - an upcoming row from a second mate carries its recorded request link to the parent
ok - a request the captain owes an answer on is never re-labelled into the waiting state
ok - a delivery that resumed and failed keeps its own state instead of reading as delivered
ok - an overdue delivery outranks recent ones so the bound never drops it
ok - a second mate's delivery reaches the parent as a delivered row with its owner and link
ok - the configured external-wait verb preserves live and exited deliveries and their nudges in both homes
ok - both homes require a declared wait, retain exited deliveries, and preserve superseding states and diagnostics
ok - both delivery projections retain approvals after green CI until resolution and reject invalid poll artifacts
ok - full GitLab request URLs survive awaiting, active, and queued child projections
ok - lookup failures preserve keyed decisions and parent evidence until verified work resumes
ok - the ledger retains every delivery and the consuming bound discloses only younger omissions
ok - status URLs neither select nonworking children nor become working-child request links
ok - backlog reason URLs never replace recorded request links or supply missing links in either home
